# scripts/opcount: `awss3bench bench calls N` makes N rounds of three S3
# calls through the generated client over an in-memory handler (wf10
# GEN-EMIT): HeadObject, GetObject of 64 KB into a sink, DeleteObject of a
# missing key. The cost of one round is the slope between the two sizes.
# The control is hand Go: net/http's Header and Request, the same handler
# logic, the answer's headers read into a struct. The floor reads each
# header once from a fixed table and hands the body over with no copy.
unit round
sizes 2000 12000
args bench calls {n}
control benchmarks/awss3/testdata/control
floor benchmarks/awss3/testdata/floor
